= Prethesis and Thesis

== Co-supervision

Some of these projects are run jointly with a colleague, in which case there are two supervisors
and the scope is agreed between the three of us. Mention it in your message if you would like to
be considered for one of those.

- *Dr. Toan-Van Nguyen*: Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering, San Diego State University, USA.
- *Assoc. Prof. Tung Kieu*: Department of Computer Science, Aalborg University, Denmark.
- *Msc. Nguyen Trung Nghia*: School of Computer Science and Engineering, International University, Vietnam.

== What I work on

My current interests include deep learning, federated learning, edge inference, collaborative
inference, semantic communication, large language models (LLM), distributed learning, deep
reinforcement learning for networks, and wireless and mobile networking with the Internet of
Things.

The easiest way to find a topic is to open the two or three most recent papers on the
Publications page and ask which one you would like to understand deeply enough to extend.

== Open topics

=== Topics you can discuss with me

- *Deep Learning and Large Language Models (LLM):* Applications in network optimization and semantic communication.
- *Federated Learning and Collaborative Inference:* Distributed training and inference across resource-constrained edge devices.
- *Edge Intelligence and Semantic Communication:* Transmitting semantic meaning rather than raw bits over limited bandwidth.
- *Deep Reinforcement Learning for Networks:* Learning control policies for wireless and mobile networking without accurate models.
- *Network Optimization and Game Theory:* Resource allocation and network utility maximization.

== How we work

- One individual meeting each week, plus a group seminar.
- You are expected to read actively, write down what you understand, and present your work
  regularly -- including the weeks when it is not going well.
- The goal is a result you can defend: a clear question, a method, and evidence.
